    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d452">

                <pb facs="d451-1" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/d451-1"/>

                <head>452. Telegram 1512 to Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d452-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1956-01-17">January 17, 1956, 8:19
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d452-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d452-1"/>
                <p>1512. For Johnson. Your 1387.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>If Wang should accept our amended draft without change and press for
                        immediate announcement, you should inform him question of <pb facs="0706"
                            n="659" type="typeset" xml:id="pg659"/> timing announcement must be
                        referred Washington and propose special meeting mutually satisfactory date
                        during week beginning January 23 to make final arrangements for release day
                        following such meeting. Department would agree to release first in Geneva
                        and by Department shortly thereafter.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>You given full discretion as to whether to refer to newspaper article Liu
                        An-hua. FYI VOA broadcasting Liu An-hua case worldwide and seeking similar
                        stories on other individuals mentioned by Wang.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d452-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d452-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 611.93/1–1756. Confidential;
                    Priority; Limit Distribution. Drafted by Clough; cleared by Sebald, Phleger in
                    draft, and McConaughy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
